1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,836
<i>Wow. I didn't know you had a fan.</i>

2
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:04,587
[BILLY] <i>I feel a sense of…</i>

3
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:05,630
<i>Potential?</i>

4
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:08,049
<i>Have you seen my red shoes?</i>

5
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,759
[PRECIOUS] <i>You're becoming so forgetful!</i>

6
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:11,261
<i>First, you lost your keys.</i>

7
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:12,971
<i>Now, it's your shoes.</i>

8
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:16,099
[BILLY]<i> I got out of the car</i>
<i>holding my shoes.</i>

9
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,559
[PRECIOUS] <i>Then where are they?</i>

10
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:19,728
[MALE OFFICER]
<i>Carlos Toledo, you're free to go.</i>

11
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:20,729
[CALOY] <i>You two again?</i>

12
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:22,063
<i>Who bailed you out?</i>

13
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,940
[CALOY]<i> I don't know!</i>

14
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:25,442
[JORDAN] <i>A taxi arrived.</i>

15
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:28,862
<i>We don't know who it was,</i>
<i>but that person handed him an envelope.</i>

16
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,322
[MARIELA]
<i>You really take after your father.</i>

17
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:33,116
[SCREAMING] <i>Ma! Ma!</i>

18
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>- Take her.</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

19
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,035
<i>Abigail!</i>

20
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:36,453
<i>Abigail!</i>

21
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:38,246
[ABI] <i>Luck is finally on our side.</i>

22
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:39,998
<i>I can feel it.</i>

23
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:43,168
[SECURITY OFFICER]
Ma'am, who are you meeting?

24
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:45,754
Oh, I'm here for Ms. Billy. My idol.

25
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:47,464
LoveList's CEO.

26
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,215
Oh, LoveList! That's upstairs, ma'am.

27
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,426
- Oh, I can go upstairs?
- Yes, ma'am.

28
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,011
[SQUEALS] Oh my gosh!

29
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:54,220
Thank you!

30
00:00:54,304 --> 00:01:00,810
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

31
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,578
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

32
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:19,954
[BLAIRE] Chief, excuse me.

33
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,623
Someone's looking for you downstairs.

34
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:24,042
But she doesn't have an appointment.

35
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:24,959
Who is it?

36
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:27,045
She said her name is Abigail Mercado.

37
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:35,804
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:16,052
Hi, miss!

39
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,012
Are you Abigail Mercado?

40
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,097
Yes.

41
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,141
Let's go upstairs.
Chief Billy is waiting for you.

42
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,268
- Ms. Billy? My idol?
- Yeah!

43
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,352
Oh, okay.

44
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,020
It's beautiful.

45
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:27,772
So people tell me.

46
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:29,691
No, not you! I meant them.

47
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,944
- All of them here.
- Oh, you meant them?

48
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:35,905
Everyone here has a pleasing personality.

49
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:37,532
Oh, them?

50
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:38,992
No, all of us, actually.

51
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:43,538
- [BILLY] Could we add--
- Chief, Ms. Abigail is here.

52
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:45,999
- Hi, Abi!
- [SQUEALS] Ms. Billy!

53
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:47,750
- Ms. Billy!
- [BILLY] Hello, how are you?

54
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:49,669
- I'm great!
- Welcome!

55
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:50,879
Welcome to LoveList!

56
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:53,089
Yes, I'm finally here!

57
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,841
This place is amazing!

58
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,426
Your office is huge!

59
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:57,385
Thank you.

60
00:02:57,468 --> 00:03:03,224
I mean, you got 323,000 subscribers
in just two years!

61
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:05,643
Your office is bound to look great!

62
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:08,938
And you even have 465,000 male hopefuls.

63
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,816
[SQUEALS] Sounds like you're
all having a lot of fun here!

64
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,110
Everyone, this is Abi.

65
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:15,236
Hello.

66
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,447
Hi, girl. I'm Toni.

67
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,990
- I'm the--
- Head of Finance!

68
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:20,950
Hmm. Hi, I'm Marj--

69
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:23,077
You're the Social Media Manager!

70
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,829
[MARJ CHUCKLES] Wow.

71
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,664
And there's Charm!

72
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:29,751
She's the Head of Design and Marketing.

73
00:03:29,834 --> 00:03:31,836
I watch all your vlogs!

74
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,254
Hmm.

75
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,506
For sure, you know him too.

76
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,091
Wow! He's handsome!

77
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:39,636
You're Jordan Valentin!

78
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:42,972
He's the only one who
developed the LoveList app.

79
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,182
- Right?
- You're right.

80
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:47,143
And he's the
head of the IT department.

81
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,478
In case you didn't know,

82
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:51,898
he went to college in Australia!
He had a full scholarship!

83
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:55,193
And he has a bar in Pobla!
Jade and Jude's!

84
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:57,195
- Wow!
- Hi, I'm Abi!

85
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,906
- Nice to meet you, Abi.
- Nice to meet you.

86
00:03:59,989 --> 00:04:02,825
[ABI CHUCKLES]

87
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,203
So, Abi, what brings you here?

88
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:08,623
Oh, I just happened to pass by,
Ms. Billy, because, well…

89
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:13,461
Didn't you say you would give me a tour
of your office when you had time?

90
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:15,463
Well, since I have time right now…

91
00:04:15,546 --> 00:04:17,215
Do you have the time?

92
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:18,466
[BILLY] Ah!

93
00:04:21,219 --> 00:04:22,136
Okay!

94
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,721
- Sure. I'll give you a tour.
- [SQUEALING]

95
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:25,265
Um, do you want anything?

96
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:28,017
We have coffee, juice, water?

97
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:29,978
- Anything!
- Wow, you have all of that?

98
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:31,562
Uh, I'll get some later!

99
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,816
Oh, but can I go to the restroom first?

100
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:35,858
Of course, of course!

101
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,694
- Please lead the way.
- Okay, ma'am.

102
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:40,363
Oh, you don't have to!
I know you're all busy.

103
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:41,739
I'll go by myself. Is it this way?

104
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,199
- Yes.
- All right, I'll go.

105
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,118
- Okay.
- He's so handsome…

106
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,577
So handsome!

107
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,329
- [ABI SQUEALS]
- Thank you!

108
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:49,414
- Oh…
- It's to your right.

109
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:50,957
- Right? Here?
- Who was that?

110
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,874
She was ogling you.

111
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:55,753
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,089
So?

113
00:04:58,631 --> 00:04:59,507
Hmm…

114
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,259
I like her.

115
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,928
It's like she's got photographic memory.

116
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:07,348
You know, we can use it
on our presentations and all.

117
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:09,475
Mm-hmm. Plus,

118
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:11,561
she doesn't seem to be a diva.

119
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:13,146
- I kinda like her!
- Mm-hmm.

120
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:14,105
I think she's good.

121
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:16,774
She said she's a marketing graduate too.

122
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:18,818
She just couldn't apply
to other companies for now

123
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:21,779
because she's managing
her mother's internet café.

124
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,492
Hm?

125
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:28,661
Cat got your tongue?

126
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:31,164
[SIGHS]

127
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:32,874
It's kinda weird, right?

128
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,752
Look, Billy.

129
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:39,255
She gave you a call
during the launch of LoveLine.

130
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:40,339
For no reason.

131
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:42,133
Then,

132
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:44,052
she went to your house

133
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,428
uninvited!

134
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:47,305
It's weird!

135
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,515
And now she's here.

136
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:50,808
Unannounced.

137
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:53,770
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:56,272
That's because she's a fan of LoveList.

139
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:57,231
Right?

140
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:58,441
It's obvious.

141
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:01,235
She keeps up with our subscriber count,

142
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:03,696
is knowledgeable about our operations,

143
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:07,825
and she knows about
our members' feedback too.

144
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:09,243
Maybe that's why.

145
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:12,830
Plus, she told me she's good
with the computer too.

146
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,665
Who knows? She could be of help to you.

147
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:16,959
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

148
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:18,169
The question is,

149
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:19,921
is she applying?

150
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:21,130
Seems not.

151
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,591
And the question is,

152
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:25,384
are we hiring?

153
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:27,345
Doesn't seem to be the case either, chief.

154
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:41,609
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

155
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:53,329
Wow!

156
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:57,959
[WHISPERS] LoveLine…

157
00:06:58,459 --> 00:06:59,836
[LAUGHS]

158
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:31,826
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

159
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:33,119
Billy?

160
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,080
I want some coffee.

161
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:41,419
Oh! I want some snacks too.

162
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:43,254
If it's possible,

163
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:46,799
can you get me
a slice of cake from downstairs?

164
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,595
And… by the way, Billy,

165
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:53,389
I don't like your work.

166
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:56,100
I don't like your attitude.

167
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,144
And most of all,

168
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:00,730
I don't like that face of yours!

169
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:03,191
So you are fired!

170
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:05,401
Where did that girl go?

171
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,195
What's taking her so long?

172
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,696
Oh, right.

173
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:10,072
Where is she?

174
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:14,118
Hi, Ms. Lindsay!

175
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:16,412
Our CEO, Ms. Billy, would like to know

176
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,415
when we can present
our investor packages to you.

177
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:23,044
[GASPS SOFTLY] Okay!
I will inform Ms. Billy.

178
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:26,714
Thank you for your interest
in investing in LoveList, Ms. Lindsay.

179
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:28,090
- Thank you.
- [ABI] Okay, okay.

180
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,384
All right. I know.

181
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:32,178
I'll give you a chance.

182
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,096
I can see your value.

183
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:37,016
Even if they can't, I can.

184
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:40,019
- So yes. I will give you a chance.
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

185
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,395
- [STAFF MEMBER] Ms. Charm?
- Yes?

186
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:42,605
Sorry, something came up.

187
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,775
Okay. Coming.

188
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:49,946
Thank you!

189
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,405
Charm?

190
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:53,157
- Chief!
- Have you seen Abi?

191
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:55,326
Huh? N-No.

192
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:59,413
I went to your office just before,
and someone was there.

193
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,374
I thought you were in a meeting.

194
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,459
What?

195
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,752
Yeah.

196
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:06,671
Let's go.

197
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:13,386
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

198
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:15,304
Abi.

199
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:17,682
Oh, Ms. Billy Idol!

200
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:20,142
I really look up to you so much!

201
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:22,687
Check out this award of yours!

202
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:25,106
"12th Annual Tech Achievement Awards:

203
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:26,774
Best Social Application."

204
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,902
This was the award you received
back in January, right?

205
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:32,363
- Mm-hmm. Yes, correct.
- I watched the livestream!

206
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:34,740
Plus, your gown was beautiful!

207
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:37,451
It's a long gown in emerald green!

208
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:38,828
You were so gorgeous.

209
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:40,204
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY] Thank you.

210
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,998
Have you been here for a long time?

211
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:44,417
Ah! Yeah…

212
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,627
I got lost after going to the bathroom.

213
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:49,213
Who were you talking to earlier?

214
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:51,424
Talking to?

215
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:53,301
Oh, no one.

216
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:54,677
I was just admiring the office.

217
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,387
Maybe you heard me singing some praises.

218
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:58,055
Ms. Billy's office is just too wonderful.

219
00:09:58,139 --> 00:09:59,890
- Mm-hmm…
- I wasn't talking to anyone.

220
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:01,517
[CHARM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

221
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:03,352
Anyway, chief,

222
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,062
I spoke with Ms. Lindsay.

223
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:08,232
I followed up with her
regarding our presentation,

224
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:12,320
and she said she'll get back
to us with her schedule.

225
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:13,654
Okay.

226
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:14,864
Thank you, Charm.

227
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:16,115
Okay.

228
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,867
- Okay. Thank you.
- [LAUGHS LIGHTLY]

229
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:18,951
Mm-hmm.

230
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:21,203
[ABI LAUGHS]

231
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:24,165
Your office is so wonderful, Ms. Billy!

232
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:25,416
Thank you.

233
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:27,376
Oh! No way!

234
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:29,003
[ABI] Could it be?

235
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:32,965
It is! It's the Spirit
of Innovation Award 2026!

236
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:35,259
It's gorgeous.
I'm finally seeing it in person.

237
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:37,428
Oh, wait. I got it wrong, Ms. Billy Idol.

238
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:39,930
Emerald isn't the color
that suits you best.

239
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,141
It's champagne. That's perfect for you!

240
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:44,852
You looked absolutely stunning
in that gown!

241
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:46,437
It's… Oh!

242
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:50,524
And your speech was so moving.
It brought me to tears.

243
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:52,151
You said,

244
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:56,197
"I'd like to thank someone
very special to me."

245
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,866
"My younger brother, Oliver."

246
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,493
"Oliver…"

247
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:05,081
"Oliver, this is for you."

248
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:08,918
"You've been my inspiration
all these years."

249
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,962
- See? I've got it memorized!
- Mm-hmm.

250
00:11:12,046 --> 00:11:13,339
[ABI GIGGLES]

251
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:17,218
The genes we inherit from our parents

252
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:22,807
determine our characteristics,
like eye color, hair type,

253
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:25,017
and even certain health conditions.

254
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:27,186
That's right! Correct, Oliver.

255
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:29,438
Now, for my next question…

256
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:33,818
Why don't children look
exactly like their parents?

257
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:39,782
Similarly, why don't siblings look
exactly the same as each other?

258
00:11:39,865 --> 00:11:42,952
You aren't the spitting image
of your siblings, right?

259
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,453
Who wants to try?

260
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,539
Uh… Biboy?

261
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:51,961
Uh…

262
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:53,462
Because…

263
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:57,425
Tsk! I don't know, ma'am.

264
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:59,218
[LAUGHTER]

265
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:01,345
[TEACHER] Don't-- Children.

266
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,848
Don't be like that.
Settle down, settle down.

267
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,891
- Ma'am, I know the answer.
- Yes, Oliver?

268
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:09,979
We don't get the same genes
as our siblings or parents.

269
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:12,815
Instead, we get
a combination of their genes.

270
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,900
That's why each of us is unique.

271
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:17,528
That's right! Correct again, Oliver.

272
00:12:17,611 --> 00:12:19,572
Let's give him a round of applause!

273
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:26,579
[APPLAUSE]

274
00:12:27,621 --> 00:12:29,582
[BIBOY WHISPERING]
That twig is such a show-off.

275
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:31,542
Why twig?

276
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:33,335
- He's skinny as a twig!
- Oh.

277
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:35,171
[BIBOY] I'll teach him a lesson later.

278
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:40,259
You keep saying that.
When will you actually do it?

279
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:41,635
Later. During recess.

280
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:46,182
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

281
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:48,434
Oliver really is my inspiration.

282
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:52,396
Everything I do here is for him.

283
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:57,943
Oliver sure is lucky.

284
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,070
Her sister loves him very much.

285
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,200
Of course.

286
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:08,496
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:12,416
What kind of person
doesn't love their sibling?

288
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,211
Plenty of people.

289
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:20,299
There are plenty of people
who don't love their siblings.

290
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:22,092
Well, that's not the case with Oliver.

291
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:25,888
He's a kind boy, and…

292
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,015
he's very smart.

293
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:31,936
He definitely takes after
his sister. [CHUCKLES]

294
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:33,979
He's also a fighter.

295
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:37,233
His biggest battle?

296
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,485
Type 1 diabetes.

297
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:41,529
Diagnosed when he was 7.

298
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:46,825
That's why we put in extra effort
into taking care of him,

299
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:51,121
especially since Auntie Pres and I
are the only family he has.

300
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:55,793
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:57,545
By the way,

302
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,797
where are your parents?

303
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:05,094
They're dead.

304
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:06,637
They're long gone.

305
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:13,519
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:15,229
[MUSIC STOPS]

307
00:14:15,312 --> 00:14:21,026
Oh, so we're in the same boat,
Ms. Billy Idol!

308
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,070
I told you before, right?

309
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:27,616
I don't have a father.
My sister's gone too.

310
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,869
It's just my mother and me.

311
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,996
- Mm-hmm.
- It's funny.

312
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:37,334
Sometimes, I think about
signing her up for LoveList

313
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:39,295
- so she can find love again.
- Mm?

314
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:42,506
- [ABI CHUCKLES]
- And speaking of LoveList,

315
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,508
I promised you a tour, right?

316
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:46,302
Let's do it. Come on.

317
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:47,636
[SQUEALS] Right now?!

318
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,264
- Yeah. Let's go?
- Oh, okay! Let's go, idol!

319
00:14:50,347 --> 00:14:51,765
[BILLY] Where do you want to start?

320
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:52,850
Oh, let's start here.

321
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:56,061
This is the LoveLine call center.

322
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:58,522
That's where we answer calls
from our members.

323
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:01,191
Usually, this area is very busy.

324
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,445
And then, over here,
that's our common area.

325
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:08,407
All the employees can get
free drinks from our café.

326
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:13,245
And the room you were just in,
that's my office.

327
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,205
[ABI] Yes, I figured. [CHUCKLES]

328
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:17,708
That's where all the magic happens.

329
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:20,502
That's where we discuss and brainstorm.

330
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,839
That's where we celebrate
small and big victories.

331
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:29,762
Up on the third floor,
we have our conference room.

332
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:33,140
Usually, we meet
with clients or investors there.

333
00:15:33,223 --> 00:15:35,893
Sometimes,
we use it for special occasions.

334
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:39,188
Oh, you're really incredible,
Ms. Billy Idol!

335
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:43,567
You were able to build
such a big business!

336
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:44,860
Congratulations!

337
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,111
[BILLY] Thank you, Abi.

338
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:48,697
Do you think I could be part of LoveList?

339
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:53,243
Because I want to learn from you.
I want to be like you.

340
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:54,453
I mean…

341
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:58,290
Are you accepting applications?
Even just as your assistant.

342
00:15:58,374 --> 00:15:59,875
I won't say no to that!

343
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,710
Sorry, but she already has an assistant.

344
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,629
And that's me.

345
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:05,089
Hi, I'm Blaire.

346
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:06,548
Nice meeting you,

347
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:09,051
even though you've been
ignoring me since earlier.

348
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:13,597
I didn't ignore you. I told you
your outfit was nice, didn't I?

349
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,057
Yeah, right.

350
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:18,060
Anyway, Chief, you have to sign this.

351
00:16:18,143 --> 00:16:19,561
This is the billing

352
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,564
for the additional computers
that are coming.

353
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:26,402
I see. Sorry, Abi.

354
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:28,445
I hope you enjoyed our mini tour.

355
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:30,781
But I have to go.
I have a lot of work to do.

356
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,408
- Thank you for visiting.
- Of course!

357
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:35,327
I really enjoyed it.
Thank you so much for your time.

358
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,955
Thank you, Ms. Billy Idol!

359
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:41,500
- [BILLY] Thank you.
- [ABI GIGGLES]

360
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:43,127
- Take care, Abi.
- I will.

361
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:45,254
- [BLAIRE] Thank you.
- Thank you. Take care.

362
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:46,171
[CHUCKLES]

363
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,840
- Be safe.
- Bye, Abi!

364
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:48,799
Hm?

365
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:51,343
[BLAIRE] Anyway, chief,
I also need your signature here

366
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:54,638
so we can follow up with the bank
about the release of your loan.

367
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:57,266
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

368
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:59,268
[BILLY] Please do follow up with them.

369
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:02,646
My loan's already approved,
but they still haven't released the check.

370
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:05,065
[BLAIRE] No worries.
I'm sure it'll be released this week.

371
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,025
Thank you.

372
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,234
[GIGGLES]

373
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:10,696
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:12,031
Guys,

375
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:15,534
Chief Billy has already reviewed
our presentation for Ms. Lindsay.

376
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:17,953
And we have revisions to do.

377
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:23,459
Oh, I hope my crystals can convince

378
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:26,462
Ms. Lindsay to invest.

379
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:27,546
[INHALES SHARPLY]

380
00:17:27,629 --> 00:17:29,757
But we're doing great, aren't we?

381
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:31,258
Right?

382
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:35,054
Of course, why are you even asking?
LoveLine has been well-received.

383
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:37,765
It translated to new members for LoveList.

384
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:41,060
We also have new ads coming in.

385
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,313
We have potential investors too.

386
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:47,149
It's just that putting up
a call center is very expensive.

387
00:17:47,232 --> 00:17:48,150
[CHARM] And…

388
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:52,404
Billy mortgaged her house for it.

389
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,365
But Billy is positive that
she will recoup her investment.

390
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,451
[TONI] Think positive!

391
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:59,286
- Think positive.
- Well, well, well.

392
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:02,873
We're really going to recoup it if…

393
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:04,166
if…

394
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:05,542
no one spoils it.

395
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:07,586
[MARJ] We just said
to think positive.

396
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:09,171
- You're so pessimistic.
- We just said so.

397
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:10,547
[PHONE RINGS]

398
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,049
- Hold it!
- Okay.

399
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:13,175
There.

400
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:14,635
[MARJ] I think you need that too.

401
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:15,677
- [TONI] Hold it.
- Hello?

402
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:16,762
- Look up.
- Who's this?

403
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:17,679
[LARRY] <i>Hello?</i>

404
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,515
This is Larry, the taxi driver.

405
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:22,643
[LARRY] <i>I heard that you called</i>
<i>the office looking for me?</i>

406
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:24,853
Yes, Mr. Larry.

407
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:26,396
Thank you for calling.

408
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,274
You said that you forgot
your wallet in my taxi.

409
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,527
[LARRY] <i>But I didn't find</i>
<i>any wallets here.</i>

410
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:33,695
Actually, sir,

411
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:36,156
I didn't call about the wallet.

412
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:39,076
I'd like to ask you something
about your passenger

413
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:42,079
last night at around 7:00 p.m.
in Tenement Road.

414
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:45,124
With how many passengers I drive,
do you think I'd remember that?

415
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,959
You will receive a reward.

416
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:49,753
You said seven last night, right?

417
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,296
Wait a minute.

418
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,549
[LARRY] <i>Ah, I remember now.</i>

419
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:55,050
<i>The beautiful woman.</i>

420
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,761
Your passenger was a woman?

421
00:18:57,845 --> 00:18:59,179
Uh…

422
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:00,764
What did she look like?

423
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,307
Can you describe her to me?

424
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:03,475
Wait a second.

425
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,977
How much is the reward?

426
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:07,396
Five thousand pesos!

427
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:08,856
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:11,066
I remember what she looked like.

429
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:13,360
As well as where I dropped her off.

430
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:14,945
Okay.

431
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,363
Where can we meet?

432
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,532
Just meet me at our garage.

433
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:21,952
But you need to hurry up.
I still have stuff to do.

434
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,328
Okay. Thank you.

435
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:24,496
Wait a minute!

436
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,331
You're going to meet with him?

437
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:29,042
Didn't Billy tell us to stop already?

438
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:32,796
Here, Jordan. That's citrine.

439
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,883
It prevents misfortune.
So you won't get hurt.

440
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:38,343
Take a deep breath. Inhale.
[INHALES DEEPLY]

441
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:39,428
Exhale. [EXHALES DEEPLY]

442
00:19:39,511 --> 00:19:41,346
- Inhale.
- Toni, Toni, Toni.

443
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,556
I don't have time for this.

444
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:44,349
But go on, just keep going.

445
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,394
Hmm? Where are you going?

446
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:48,312
[JORDAN] Uh…

447
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:50,647
Just out to get a coffee.

448
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:53,442
- Mm.
- Ahh.

449
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:56,403
[IN UNISON] Coffee…

450
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,655
Mm.

451
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,032
So, where are you going?

452
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:02,409
Fine.

453
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:05,662
I spoke with the taxi driver already.

454
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:07,331
He agreed to meet.

455
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:10,876
He'll describe the person
he dropped off at Caloy's house.

456
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,836
Chief, he said it was a woman.

457
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:15,339
- A woman?
- Mm.

458
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:17,799
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

459
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:18,967
Okay, Jordan.

460
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:22,512
I know I was impulsive myself.
I admit that.

461
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:25,432
But this is a different story.
Didn't you get stabbed?

462
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:30,020
Maybe we need to let
the authorities handle this.

463
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:30,979
[JORDAN] Dude.

464
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:33,815
You know that won't achieve anything.

465
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:35,651
The authorities move so slowly.

466
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:37,653
It's just like with my mom's case.

467
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:40,197
Until now, no one has been arrested.

468
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,949
No one has been punished!

469
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:48,830
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:51,166
Okay, let's do
the circulatory system this time.

471
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,085
What organs are involved?

472
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:56,713
Heart, blood vessels, blood…

473
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:58,548
One more! I taught you this, right?

474
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,509
- One more! You can do it.
- One more?

475
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:03,262
Oh, I remember now! Lungs.

476
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:05,472
- Very good. You did great.
- [GIGGLES]

477
00:21:05,555 --> 00:21:07,266
- Let's eat first.
- Okay.

478
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:09,101
Just don't forget those, okay?

479
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:11,144
[SUZIE] I have cupcakes. Take one.

480
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:12,521
Uh…

481
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:13,772
I'm not allowed to eat those.

482
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:16,233
My mom baked these for me.

483
00:21:16,316 --> 00:21:19,486
I also requested one for you.
Low sugar, low carb!

484
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:21,530
- Wow, how nice of you.
- [GIGGLES]

485
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:22,489
So, which one is it?

486
00:21:22,572 --> 00:21:23,615
[SUZIE] It's this one here.

487
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:25,284
Thank you. Are you sure?

488
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,077
- Sure!
- [CHUCKLES]

489
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:29,329
- Do you want us to share?
- Okay.

490
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:31,039
Here's yours.

491
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:37,671
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,965
Mm! It tastes really good.

493
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:43,427
[BIBOY'S FRIEND] There he is!
Go, eat his food!

494
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:45,554
- It tastes good.
- There he is.

495
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,180
- Go, eat it!
- [SNICKERS]

496
00:21:49,057 --> 00:21:50,976
- There you go!
- That's not yours!

497
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:52,936
- Is it delicious, bro?
- How selfish!

498
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:54,938
- [SNICKERING]
- Whoa!

499
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:56,523
[LAUGHING]

500
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:58,025
[OLIVER] Suzie, are you all right?

501
00:21:58,108 --> 00:21:59,526
- [SNICKERING]
- Oh!

502
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:00,819
Twig is getting mad already!

503
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:02,446
[BIBOY AND FRIENDS] Twig! Twig!

504
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:03,739
That's enough!

505
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:04,823
Let's just leave, Suzie.

506
00:22:04,906 --> 00:22:06,742
What? You're not fighting back?

507
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,744
Well, that's what you'd expect
from a twig! Twig!

508
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,078
[BIBOY'S FRIENDS LAUGHING]

509
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:12,331
- [GROANS]
- Ooh! He got hit!

510
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:13,790
- Nice hit!
- You're really good, bro!

511
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:16,126
- There you go!
- That's what I like to see!

512
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:18,045
You're really great, bro.

513
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:19,755
- [GRUNTS]
- Oh!

514
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:21,173
- Bro!
- Hey, bro!

515
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:23,675
Hey! What's going on here? Stop that!

516
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:26,094
- Are you all right, bro?
- Are you all right, bro?

517
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:27,387
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

518
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:28,764
Jordan!

519
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:36,772
How can you be sure
the taxi driver will tell the truth?

520
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,940
I think he'll cooperate.

521
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:42,486
If not, I'll make him.

522
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:44,988
What if he's working with Caloy?

523
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,656
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

524
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:50,744
Billy, this taxi driver is
our best shot right now.

525
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:55,332
He's our only lead to the woman
who gave him the money.

526
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:58,794
[JORDAN] Whoever she is,
I won't let her ruin LoveList.

527
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:00,837
I won't let her do that to us.

528
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:02,631
To you.

529
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:06,343
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

530
00:23:06,426 --> 00:23:07,302
You guys are leaving?

531
00:23:07,385 --> 00:23:08,553
Uh…

532
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,347
[VALERIE] Don't we have a meeting

533
00:23:10,430 --> 00:23:12,557
to discuss our social media strategy?

534
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:15,352
Yes, we do.

535
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:16,853
Toni will lead the meeting.

536
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,855
Sorry, we just need to do something.

537
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,023
[VALERIE] Ah, where?

538
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:21,942
Sorry, Val. We're running late.

539
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:26,613
[JORDAN] Do you think it's her?

540
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:30,367
I don't think the taxi driver
was referring to her.

541
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:32,869
I know she can be scheming sometimes,

542
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:35,330
but I don't think she's the type
of person who'd conspire

543
00:23:35,413 --> 00:23:37,290
with someone like Caloy.

544
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:39,668
- I hope so.
- [PHONE RINGS]

545
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:41,336
- We'll find out soon.
- Wait.

546
00:23:41,419 --> 00:23:42,587
Hello?

547
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:47,175
Okay, I will.

548
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,593
Yes, ma'am. I'm on my way.

549
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:52,347
Oliver got into a fight.

550
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:54,182
- I'll just go to his school.
- Wait, Oliver?

551
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:55,142
Did he get hurt?

552
00:23:55,225 --> 00:23:57,144
I hope not. They didn't tell me.

553
00:23:57,227 --> 00:23:58,895
- I'll take care of it.
- Are you sure?

554
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:01,439
Okay then.

555
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:04,025
I'll meet with the taxi driver. Okay?

556
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:04,943
Be careful, okay?

557
00:24:05,026 --> 00:24:06,319
You too.

558
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:11,408
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

559
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:20,250
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

560
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:24,754
Good afternoon, sir.

561
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:26,131
I'm Jordan.

562
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:27,841
Where's Mr. Larry?

563
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:29,759
Oh, I'm sorry.

564
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:31,261
You missed him.

565
00:24:31,344 --> 00:24:32,304
He just left.

566
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:34,723
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

567
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:36,975
- Okay, thank you.
- All right.

568
00:24:40,937 --> 00:24:42,105
[CALOY] Boss.

569
00:24:43,607 --> 00:24:44,816
Boss!

570
00:24:46,026 --> 00:24:47,527
Are you Jordan?

571
00:24:50,739 --> 00:24:52,157
Hey! What are you doing?

572
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,950
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

573
00:24:54,034 --> 00:24:55,869
If you say anything to that man,

574
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,037
I'll finish you off!

575
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:58,747
- Caloy!
- And your family--

576
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:00,207
Let him go.

577
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:05,086
[LARRY] If you have a problem,
don't drag me into it!

578
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:15,430
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

579
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,186
[BILLY] <i>What happened?</i>

580
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:22,103
<i>I got into a fight.</i>

581
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:24,147
[MAN] <i>Your brother</i>
<i>is a delinquent.</i>

582
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:27,859
[BILLY] <i>A kid defending himself</i>
<i>doesn't make him a delinquent.</i>

583
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:29,569
[CALOY] <i>You still haven't</i>
<i>learned your lesson?</i>

584
00:25:29,653 --> 00:25:31,529
<i>Who's your boss?</i>
<i>Tell me!</i>

585
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:34,407
<i>Passing that checklist of yours</i>
<i>is an impossible task.</i>

586
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:35,450
<i>Huh?</i>

587
00:25:35,533 --> 00:25:36,701
<i>I'd never put you in danger.</i>

588
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:38,828
<i>I dare you to show</i>
<i>your messages and calls.</i>

589
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,538
[BILLY]
<i>You are so stubborn!</i>

590
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:41,998
<i>Dude, I'm sorry.</i>

591
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:43,250
<i>You don't have to apologize.</i>

592
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:45,585
<i>You only did that for…</i>

593
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:46,753
<i>For us.</i>

594
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:47,712
<i>Aww!</i>

595
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:51,091
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
